188415	281835	\N	Female	+91 8087994886	\N	NIKHAT NAZIM QURESHI	\N	ANA (by IFA)	Pathology	06-06-2026 18:07	10-06-2026	06-06-2026	1059157	\N	\N	bgl-Madhav	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	06-06-2026	10-06-2026	Comments	Qualitative ANA antibodies by IFA is a screening test to detect autoantibodies against cell nuclei, DNA, RNA, several proteins and ribonuclear proteins in human sera. It is deemed positive if antibodies are detected at a minimum of 1:40 dilution.\n\tThis test is a sensitive indicator for diagnosis of SLE and is recommended by American College of Rheumatologists, Sub-committee, as a screening test. However, the test has low specificity as it may be found positive in many other connective tissue disorders such as Rheumatoid Arthritis, Scleroderma and Dermatomyositis etc. Low titre positivity has been found in some other diseases such as viral infections and even in some healthy individuals specially in elderly.\n\tThis low specificity warrants that all ANA IFA positive samples should be tested by more specific tests for autoantibodies against double stranded DNA, and extractable nuclear antibodies as well as more specific tests such as ANA profile.\n\tA single positive test needs to be followed up and no treatment is warranted if negative results are obtained specially over a time period repeatedly. However, a clinical correlation is a must and interpretation of test results must be in light of clinical presentation.\n\nCorrelate Clinically.	Cantonment Hospital	\N
