168260	282330	\N	Male	+91 9881595994	\N	SHAHAJI HINGE	\N	LIVER FUNCTION TEST ( LFT )	Pathology	09-06-2026 11:37	09-06-2026	09-06-2026	979160	\N	Liver Panel	bgl-Madhav	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	09-06-2026	09-06-2026	&nbsp	BILIRUBIN levels may rise due to hepatitis, hemolysis, failure of conjugating mechanism in the liver, obstruction in the biliary system. Increase in ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE (ALP) activity is an index of cholestasis, a blockage of bile flow. Increase in ALP may also occur in infiltrative diseases of the liver and cirrhosis. TRANSAMINASES(GOT and GPT) are a measure of the integrity of liver cells. They are elevated in acute damage to hepatocytes irrespective of etiology. The causes include – hepatitis, toxic injury, drug overdose, shock, severe hypoxia. A decrease in SERUM TOTAL PROTEINS indicates a decrease in the liver’s synthetic capacity and thus indicates the severity of the liver disease.	SHITAL GHODKE	\N
