184340	281613	\N	Female	+91 9595601190	\N	ANJUM SHAIKH	\N	LIVER FUNCTION TEST ( LFT )	Pathology	05-06-2026 16:50	05-06-2026	05-06-2026	1185156	\N	Liver Panel	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	05-06-2026	05-06-2026	&nbsp	BILIRUBIN levels may rise due to hepatitis, hemolysis, failure of conjugating mechanism in the liver, obstruction in the biliary system. Increase in ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE (ALP) activity is an index of cholestasis, a blockage of bile flow. Increase in ALP may also occur in infiltrative diseases of the liver and cirrhosis. TRANSAMINASES(GOT and GPT) are a measure of the integrity of liver cells. They are elevated in acute damage to hepatocytes irrespective of etiology. The causes include – hepatitis, toxic injury, drug overdose, shock, severe hypoxia. A decrease in SERUM TOTAL PROTEINS indicates a decrease in the liver’s synthetic capacity and thus indicates the severity of the liver disease.	RGH Yerwada	\N
