141796	281401	\N	Female	+91 8668723687	\N	AFRIN SHAIKH	\N	ANTI MULLERIAN HORMONE ( AMH )	Pathology	05-06-2026 09:57	05-06-2026	05-06-2026	883156	\N	ANTI MULLERIAN HORMONE ( AMH )	bgl-Madhav	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	05-06-2026	05-06-2026	Interpretative Value:	Ovarian Fertility \n\t\t\tAMH Level in ng/mL\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOptimal Fertility \n\t\t\t 4.00 - 6.80\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSatisfactory Fertility\n\t\t\t2.20 - 3.99\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLow Fertlilty\n\t\t\t0.30 - 2.19\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tVery low/ Undetectable\n\t\t\t0.00 - 0.29\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHigh Level\n\t\t\t> 6.80\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n \n\n\n\tAnti-Mullerian Hormone or MIS (Mullerian Inhibiting Substance) is produced by the ovarian follicles.\n\tMH levels are directly proportional to the number of antral follicles in the Ovaries . Women with lower AMH have lower antral follicular counts and are known to produce a lower number of Oocytes compared with women with higher levels.\n\tAMH levels do not change significantly throughout the menstrual cycle and decrease with age. Healthy women, below 38 years old, with normal follicular status at day 3 of the menstrual cycle, have AMH levels of 2.0 - 6.8 ng/mL.\n\tAMH can be used for Evaluating Fertility Potential and ovarian response in IVF - Serum AMH levels correlate with the number of early antral follicles. This makes is useful for predicting the ovarian response in an IVF cycle. Women with low AMH levels are more likely to be poor ovarian responders.\n\tMeasuring Ovarian Aging - Women with poor ovarian reserve who have entered the menopause have low levels of AMH.\n\n\nCorrelate Clinically.	NATRAJ GHUTE	\N
