156341	274204	\N	Female	\N	\N	ZUFSHA SAYYED JAVED	\N	LIVER FUNCTION TEST ( LFT )	Pathology	29-04-2026 15:28	29-04-2026	29-04-2026	890119	\N	Liver Panel	bgl-Madhav	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	29-04-2026	29-04-2026	&nbsp	BILIRUBIN levels may rise due to hepatitis, hemolysis, failure of conjugating mechanism in the liver, obstruction in the biliary system. Increase in ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE (ALP) activity is an index of cholestasis, a blockage of bile flow. Increase in ALP may also occur in infiltrative diseases of the liver and cirrhosis. TRANSAMINASES(GOT and GPT) are a measure of the integrity of liver cells. They are elevated in acute damage to hepatocytes irrespective of etiology. The causes include – hepatitis, toxic injury, drug overdose, shock, severe hypoxia. A decrease in SERUM TOTAL PROTEINS indicates a decrease in the liver’s synthetic capacity and thus indicates the severity of the liver disease.	RGH Yerwada	\N
