181824	271040	\N	Female	+91 9132021717	\N	RUTUJA JASUL	\N	GLYCOSYLATED HAEMOGLOBIN (  HBA1c )	Pathology	14-04-2026 11:22	14-04-2026	14-04-2026	463104	\N	Glycosylated Hemoglobin HBA1C	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	14-04-2026	14-04-2026	&nbsp;	Note: Glycosylated hemoglobin (hemoglobin A1c, HbA1c, A1C, or Hb1c) is a form of hemoglobin used primarily to identify the average plasma glucose concentration over prolonged periods of time. Glycation of hemoglobin has been associated with cardiovascular disease, nephropathy and retinopathy in diabetes mellitus. HbA1c provides an index of average blood glucose levels over the past 8 -12 weeks and is a much better indicator of long term glycemic control as compared to blood anf urinary glucose determinations. A large change in mean blood glucose can increase HbA1c levels within 1-2 weeks. Sudden changes in HbA1c may occur because recent changes in blood glucose levels contribute relatively more to the final HbA1c levels than earlier events.	RGH Yerwada	\N
