181805	270992	\N	Female	\N	\N	RITU SHINDE	\N	CK MB  (CREATINE KINASE - MB)	Pathology	13-04-2026 23:46	14-04-2026	13-04-2026	895103	\N	CREATINE PHOSPHOKINASE	bgl-Nadira	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	13-04-2026	14-04-2026	&nbsp;	1. CPK-MB Mass is a cardiac marker which assists in the diagnosis of Acute Myocardial Infarction (AMI).\n2. Elevated levels of CPK-MB occur 4 to 6 hours after the onset of pain in myocardial infarction, peak at 18 to 24 hours and persist upto 72 hours.\n\n3. The decline in CPK-MB follows a predictable course & if the decline shows a sudden increase, it is suggestive of re-infarction.\n\n4. It may also be elevated in cases of Myocarditis, disorders of Skeletal muscle (trauma, intramuscular injections, vigorous exercise,\n\ndermatomyositis, Muscular dystrophy, rhabomyolysis), Stroke, Carbon monoxide poisoning, Pulmonary embolism, Hypothyroidism, etc.	Cantonment Hospital	\N
