80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	CA -125 ( OVARIAN CANCER MARKER )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	23-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	CA 12-5	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	22-07-2026	23-07-2026	&nbsp;	CA 125 is high. Please correlate clinically. CA-125 is used to monitor therapy during treatment for Ovarian Cancer. Ca-125 is also used to detect whether cancer has come back after treatment is complete. This test is sometimes used to follow High-Risk women who have a family history of Ovarian Cancer. CA-125 may normally be increased in early pregnancy and during menstruation. It can also be increased in diseases such as Pelvic Inflammatory Disease or Endometriosis and sometimes in Hepatitis and Cirrhosis of the liver. Test Method & Instrument: Test conducted on Fully Automated ImmunoAssay Analyser 'Cobas E411' from Roche Diagnostics, Germany based on ElectroChemiLuminescence (ECLIA) technology.	Cantonment Hospital	\N
80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	bgl-Madhav	Test With Descriptive Range	-	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	LDH (Lactate Dehydrogenase)	454	Cantonment Hospital	\N
80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	bgl-Madhav	Test With Normal Range	135 - 214	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	LDH (Lactate Dehydrogenase)	-	Cantonment Hospital	\N
80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE ( LDH )	bgl-Madhav	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	22-07-2026	22-07-2026	&nbsp;	Comments:\n1. Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) is a nonspecific enzyme found in most organs. Highest concentrations are found in liver, heart, muscle, kidney, lung and erythrocytes.\n2. This assay is useful for investigating a variety of diseases involving these organs.\n3. To monitor tumor activity involving anemias and lung cancer.It is also used to monitor changes in tumor burden after chemotherapy.\n4. LDH measurements are used in the diagnosis and treatments of liver diseases like Acute viral hepatitis, Cirrhosis & Metastatic carcinoma; Cardiac diseases like Myocardial infarction; Tumors of lungs / kidneys & Hematologic disorders like Megaloblastic anemia & Hemolytic anemia.	Cantonment Hospital	\N
80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	CA 19.9 ( PANCREATIC CANCER MARKER )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	23-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	\N	bgl-Irfan	Test With Normal Range	0.0 - 37.0	22-07-2026	23-07-2026	CA 19.9	5.39	Cantonment Hospital	\N
80162	292316	\N	Female	+91 8149635577	\N	Malti Popat Raut	\N	CA 19.9 ( PANCREATIC CANCER MARKER )	Pathology	22-07-2026 14:46	23-07-2026	22-07-2026	1185203	\N	\N	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	22-07-2026	23-07-2026	Note	Low amounts of CA 19-9 can be detected in healthy people, and many conditions that affect the liver or pancreas can cause temporary elevations. Moderate to high levels are found in pancreatic cancer, other cancers, and in several other diseases and conditions. The highest levels of CA 19-9 are seen in cancer of the exocrine pancreas. This cancer arises in the tissues that produce food-digesting enzymes and in the ducts that carry those enzymes into the small intestine. About 95% of pancreatic cancers are of this type. Serial measurements of CA 19-9 may be useful during and following cancer treatment. Rising or falling levels may give the doctor important information about whether the treatment is working, whether all of the cancer was removed successfully during surgery, and whether the cancer is recurring. CA19-9 can be elevated in many types of gastrointestinal cancer, such as colorectal cancer, esophageal cancer and hepatocellular carcinoma. Apart from cancer, elevated levels may also occur in pancreatitis, cirrhosis, and diseases of the bile ducts. It can be elevated in people with obstruction of the bile ducts.	Cantonment Hospital	\N
