195125	292724	\N	Female	+91 8956742091	\N	NARGIS KHAN	\N	LIPASE	Pathology	24-07-2026 10:58	24-07-2026	24-07-2026	1076205	\N	Lipase	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	24-07-2026	24-07-2026	&nbsp;	COMMENTS:\nPancreas is the major and primary source of serum lipase though lipases are also present in\nliver, stomach, intestine, WBCs, fat cells and milk. In acute pancreatitis, serum lipase becomes elevated at the same time as \namylase and remains high for 7-10 days. Increased lipase activity rarely lasts longer than 14 days. Prolonged increase suggests \npoor prognosis or presence of a cyst. The combined use of serum lipase and serum amylase is effective in ruling out acute \npancreatitis.\n\n\nIncreased levels:\n1. Acute & Chronic pancreatitis.\n2. Obstruction of pancreatic duct.\n3. Non pancreatic conditions like renal diseases, acute cholecystitis, intestinal obstruction, duodenal ulcer, alcoholism, diabetic \nketoacidosis and following endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography.	SHITAL GHODKE	\N
