195121	292719	\N	Female	\N	\N	KANTABAI KAMBLE	\N	RA FACTOR ( RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS FACTOR )   	Pathology	24-07-2026 10:48	24-07-2026	24-07-2026	1071205	\N	Rheumatoid Factor	bgl-Irfan	Descriptive (No Ranges)	-	24-07-2026	24-07-2026	&nbsp;	Rheumatoid factor is an antibody that is detectable in the blood of 80% of adults with rheumatoid arthritis.Rheumatoid can be detected in the blood of normal individuals and of those with other autoimmune diseases that are not rheumatoid arthritis.In people with rheumatoid arthritis, high levels of rheumatoid factor can indicate a tendency toward more aggressive disease and/or a tendency to develop rheumatoid nodules and rheumatoid lung disease.Rheumatoid factor is also present in patients with other conditions, including other connective tissue diseases (such as systemic lupuserythematosus), some infectious diseases (such as infectious hepatitis, syphilis, infectious mononucleosis, parasites, and tuberculosis), liver disease, and sarcoidosis. Rheumatoid factor can also sometimes be present in normal individuals without diseases. This occurs more frequently in people with family members who have rheumatoid arthritis.	RGH YERWADA NPMC	\N
